From: allolive <160342668+allolive@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 20 Sep 2026 23:20:00 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] GUIMediaWindow: read the first directory off the app thread

CGUIMediaWindow::GetDirectoryItems already knows how to list a directory on a
worker behind the busy dialog, and uses it for every navigation the window
does. OnInitWindow turns it off for the first one:

    // initial fetch is done unthreaded to ensure the items are setup prior to
    // skin animations kicking off
    m_backgroundLoad = false;

So entering a window is the one listing that runs on the app thread, and on a
network source it takes the UI with it for as long as the server needs. Opening
a TV show over NFS is exactly this path.

Use the background path for the first fetch too. The window opens and fills
rather than opening filled, which is what the removed comment was protecting -
the items are no longer guaranteed to be in place before the skin's open
animation starts. That ordering is a look, not a correctness property, and it
is already how the window behaves on every later navigation.

Stop setting the flag back to true further down; it is true from the top now.

This is the OnInitWindow half of the old 9002, which the 2026-09-13 audit of
the shelved patches picked out as the part worth keeping.

Signed-off-by: allolive <160342668+allolive@users.noreply.github.com>

diff --git a/xbmc/windows/GUIMediaWindow.cpp b/xbmc/windows/GUIMediaWindow.cpp
index 05f03d3..05ad053 100644
--- a/xbmc/windows/GUIMediaWindow.cpp
+++ b/xbmc/windows/GUIMediaWindow.cpp
@@ -1690,8 +1690,9 @@ void CGUIMediaWindow::OnRenameItem(int iItem)
 
 void CGUIMediaWindow::OnInitWindow()
 {
-  // initial fetch is done unthreaded to ensure the items are setup prior to skin animations kicking off
-  m_backgroundLoad = false;
+  // Read the first directory the way every later navigation reads one. Unthreaded
+  // it runs on the app thread, so a network source takes the UI with it.
+  m_backgroundLoad = true;
 
   // the start directory may change during Refresh
   bool updateStartDirectory = URIUtils::PathEquals(m_vecItems->GetPath(), m_startDirectory, true);
@@ -1719,8 +1720,6 @@ void CGUIMediaWindow::OnInitWindow()
     SetHistoryForPath(m_startDirectory);
   }
 
-  m_backgroundLoad = true;
-
   CGUIWindow::OnInitWindow();
 }
 
